\tag{fdip}
\title{A direction form from the Laplacian}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{A linear operator on functions that kills constants determines a
quadratic form on the outgoing edges at each site. The sign is fixed
once: the off-diagonal entries of the operator are the weights. The
operator of opposite sign produces the opposite form.}

\p{The rows of \ref{fdip-00O5} apply to this derived form, and the
declared form is the special case recorded in \ref{fdip-00PH}.}

\transclude{fdip-00PA}
